{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"05ba8f60-00b3-48d8-99ab-c36374a36e4f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fixed Generator (`gen.py`)**:\n   In [`gen.py`](file:///tmp/h-8Bt5eR/gen.py#L10-L14), updated `hr_target()` to use `\"start\"` instead of `\"value\"` for the lower bound:\n   ```python\n   def hr_target(step):\n       \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n       lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n       return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n   ```\n\n2. **Explanation Recorded in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-8Bt5eR/ANSWER.md)**:\n   Documented the exact change and why: Intervals.icu treats target dictionaries shaped as `{\"value\": ..., \"end\": ...}` as zone-mapped targets (Lap-HR mode), causing Garmin to clamp corridors to the watch's internal zones. Changing the lower bound key to `{\"start\": ..., \"end\": ...}` switches Intervals to export an Instant-HR corridor, preserving the exact raw bpm ranges computed from `%lthr`.\n","duration_seconds":248.032904,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":174600,"output_tokens":2197,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":1084933,"total_tokens":176797}}}
